insert into public.cpl_memory (slug,kind,title,summary,tags,status,source,verified_by,verified_at,author,event_date) values
('m-collection-s748','milestone','S748''s collection: 41 records','S748 (2026-11-28, the routine''s 06:12Z run): 41 records collected and live, 24 by guarded plans (21 named gaps, 3 read coverage true) and 17 by rereads and loads, no outline rows, paid reads about $0.34. The land #3945 (cd464091) carries 33; Mt. San Antonio''s eight ride a second land. No display build ran; the next run builds one for the 41.',array['program-requirements','collection','milestone'],'proposed','docs/session_749_handoff.md',null,null,'SkyStilt (S748)','2026-11-28'),
('d-no-display-build-at-start-s748','decision','No display build at S748''s start: S746''s build was current','S748 conductor: the brief''s first item, a display build, was not run at the start. S746''s #3927 applied build 229a759101f7 to 18,751 records at 01:29Z on 2026-11-28 (run 46092611343), after S742''s records closed, so the build was current. A build carrying S748''s 41 records, gate college Glendale, then the census, is the next run''s first item.',array['program-requirements','display','conductor','decision'],'proposed','docs/session_749_handoff.md',null,null,'SkyStilt (S748)','2026-11-28'),
('d-list-minimum-units-refused-s748','decision','The reconcile kind list_minimum_units was refused and removed','S748 conductor: a new reconcile kind, list_minimum_units, drafted for East Los Angeles 31017, got NO GO from its Fable reader and was removed (16f341f6) with no second round. Its pass came from a ceiling the catalog does not print: the page''s Subtotal 20-27 gives the degree 54-61 around the printed 60. 31017 stays held for a person.',array['program-requirements','reconcile','east-los-angeles','decision'],'proposed','docs/session_749_handoff.md',null,null,'SkyStilt (S748)','2026-11-28'),
('d-census-change-left-out-s748','decision','The census reading college-named gap files was left out of S748''s land','S748 conductor: the census change (claude/s748-keys 50bedbf7; 3,927 becomes 3,849) was reverted in the land on its reader''s FIX THEN LAND. None of its 78 has a live row or checks.gaps (68 place no listed course, 2 extraction errors, 8 no record), and Passing now would read 16,433 for 16,355. Fix: keep the 78 under their own cause; apply only where no live row exists; pin main()''s hand-in.',array['program-requirements','census','conductor','decision'],'proposed','docs/session_749_handoff.md',null,null,'SkyStilt (S748)','2026-11-28'),
('d-found-pages-probe-held-s748','decision','The found-pages paid probe is held until round 2; the free Skyline capture ran','S748 conductor: the found-pages change (claude/s748-readers-found e77ff6a8, off for every college) got GO WITH, the paid probe held. The extract function answers 400 on an empty closed list, and a record scored against zero listed courses passes on arithmetic alone (966 of 974 rescored still pass). The free Skyline capture ran on -found-skyline so round 2 has its sources.',array['program-requirements','found-pages','skyline','decision'],'proposed','docs/session_749_handoff.md',null,null,'SkyStilt (S748)','2026-11-28'),
('o-found-pages-194-programs-s748','opportunity','194 programs at 14 colleges have a found own page and no closed list','S748: the capture''s lookup finds the own page of a program with no closed list, and nothing files it as the source (S652''s slice B, never built). 194 programs at 14 colleges, about $19 on the estimator: Skyline 55, Allan Hancock 27, San Mateo 21, Diablo Valley 20, San Joaquin Delta 14, Gavilan 12, Glendale 12 and seven smaller. The largest lever S748 found; round 2 is in the lane''s NEXT (3).',array['program-requirements','found-pages','lever','opportunity'],'proposed','docs/session_749_handoff.md',null,null,'SkyStilt (S748)','2026-11-28'),
('d-sierra-21525-not-reread-s748','decision','Sierra 21525 was not reread: a tie, and neither record passes','S748 conductor: keep-better reads Sierra 21525 as a tie on every step and neither record passes (18 units, no total, the section cut off after IT 0060). No reread was dispatched, since it would rewrite twelve live records for no gain. The work is on claude/s748-post-sierra (f26375bd); the record waits on a person''s look.',array['program-requirements','sierra','keep-better','decision'],'proposed','docs/session_749_handoff.md',null,null,'SkyStilt (S748)','2026-11-28'),
('d-canyons-37868-not-rerun-s748','decision','College of the Canyons 37868''s failed paid read was not rerun','S748 conductor: College of the Canyons 37868''s paid read 46121986278 (claude/s748-paid-coc) failed and was not rerun, under d-west-valley-no-blind-rerun-s727: a read whose result is unexplained is never rerun blind. The next run reads the run''s log first.',array['program-requirements','college-of-the-canyons','paid-read','decision'],'proposed','docs/session_749_handoff.md',null,null,'SkyStilt (S748)','2026-11-28'),
('d-hancock-s681-entry-is-lane-assignment-s748','decision','collection_lane.py''s S681 Allan Hancock entry is a lane assignment, not a person''s hold','S748 conductor, on s748g1''s plan reader: kb/collection_lane.py''s S681 entry for Allan Hancock is a lane assignment no session lifted, not a person''s hold, so plan s748g1 applied its seven Allan Hancock named gaps (migrate 46124310448). Allan Hancock 19928''s gap may come from the reading (HUSV 120 and 170 may be alternatives): a person compares.',array['program-requirements','allan-hancock','collection-lane','decision'],'proposed','docs/session_749_handoff.md',null,null,'SkyStilt (S748)','2026-11-28'),
('p-recall-oracle-restates-rule-s748','pitfall','A recall whose oracle restates its rule cannot report a wrong','S748: twice in one night a recall''s oracle restated the rule under test (the staging fix''s test 4c; the found-pages recall, whose wrong 0 was structural, the honest figure 1 wrong in 1,969 found), and twice a plan''s test stayed green with a guard removed (s748k1, part of s748b). Every brief now asks for an oracle independent of the rule and a test that turns red on each guard''s removal.',array['program-requirements','recall','tests','pitfall'],'proposed','docs/session_749_handoff.md',null,null,'SkyStilt (S748)','2026-11-28'),
('f-yield-from-census-gaps-s748','fact','S748''s yield came from the census''s largest gaps, not the brief''s named lists','S748: the brief''s named lists were largely collected already (Santa Ana, Copper Mountain, Ventura and Norco in S741; Los Angeles Pierce and Grossmont as college-named gaps). The yield came from ranking the census''s gap by college (Sierra 99, Skyline 93, Allan Hancock 87, Mt. San Antonio 83, mostly no closed list or page not found) and sending workers there.',array['program-requirements','census','collection','fact'],'proposed','docs/session_749_handoff.md',null,null,'SkyStilt (S748)','2026-11-28'),
('p-worker-handback-repeats-s748','pitfall','A worker that leaves background jobs running hands back more than once','S748: a worker that ends its turn with background jobs still running hands back again as each job ends, and the conductor reads the same report twice. A reader''s brief says to report once, after its background jobs have ended.',array['conductor','workers','brief','pitfall'],'proposed','docs/session_749_handoff.md',null,null,'SkyStilt (S748)','2026-11-28'),
('f-harness-pins-worker-to-worktree-s748','fact','The harness pins a worker to its own worktree','S748: the harness gives each worker its own git worktree and refuses a git command it cannot verify stays inside it (a compound command, a script wrapped around git). A worker runs plain, separate git commands from its worktree, checks out the named branch there, and pushes to that branch alone.',array['conductor','workers','git','fact'],'proposed','docs/session_749_handoff.md',null,null,'SkyStilt (S748)','2026-11-28')
on conflict (slug) do nothing;

